A DRIVER TRAP MEASURED HERE, FOR THE NEXT RUN
----------------------------------------------
`show trigger` with no triggers defined prints `% No triggers currently defined`.  That is
INFORMATIONAL OUTPUT OF A SUCCESSFUL `show`, but it begins with `% `, so `cfg.py` treats it as
a CLI rejection and stops the batch (`!!! CLI error on 'show trigger' -- stopping`, exit 2,
work/w-s1-down.log).  It is NOT added to `console.ADVISORY`: that list is for `% ` lines that
accompany a successful CONFIGURATION command, and widening it to cover `show` output would
blunt the guard.  The right fix is the one applied for the rest of this case -- **run `show`
commands through `ckcon.py`, not through `cfg.py`**.  No measurement was lost: `show trigger`
was the last command of that batch and its output is in the transcript.

