=================================================================================
STEP 6 -- THE ACTION: the trigger runs its script list, proven from the log
=================================================================================
Designed expectation: a trigger's action is a script from its 1-5 script list.  No `.scp` file
exists on the DUT's flash and none can be put there from this seat (see NOT MEASURED).  But
the ATTEMPT is observable: `console.ADVISORY` already records that
`script N <file>` on a non-existent file is an ADVISORY and the reference IS stored, so a
deliberately absent file turns "did the trigger run its action?" into a question the DUT's own
log answers.

    awplus(config)# trigger 1
    awplus(config-trigger)# active                      <- re-arm trigger 1 only
    awplus(config-trigger)# script 1 flash:/cktrig.scp
    % Script /flash/cktrig.scp does not exist. Please ensure it is created before the trigger
      is activated
        (advisory, not an error -- continuing)
    awplus(config-trigger)# end

    awplus# show trigger 1
    Active ...................... Yes
    Number of activations ....... 1
    Number of scripts ........... 1
      1. flash:/cktrig.scp
      2. <not configured>
      ...
    The reference is stored, exactly as console.ADVISORY says.
    Trigger 2 was deliberately left `no active`, so the following up event is also a control.

    capture: tools/tb capture tb277 ckmgmt eth3 110 t33416-script.pcap udp port 162
    awplus(config)# interface port1.0.2 / shutdown / end   ... then ... no shutdown

    Trigger ..................... 1
    Number of activations ....... 2                            <- fired again
    Last activation ............. Mon Oct 19 23:26:46 2026
    Trigger ..................... 2
    Number of activations ....... 1
    Last activation ............. Mon Oct 19 23:20:47 2026     <- UNCHANGED: still inactive

THE DUT'S OWN LOG, VERBATIM (work/w-s7-after.log), which is the evidence for this step:

